# Kimi K2.8 Preview — findings by Mercury 3 (SELF-EXCLUDED: no verified public benchmarks)

- Source: Moonshot AI (Kimi K2.8 Preview)
- Date: 2026-11-06 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`
- Status: **`.md.excluded`** — zero verified public benchmark numbers found for this exact model/ID; scores inside are ignored by `pnpm sync`.

## Model card

- **Name:** Kimi K2.8 Preview
- **Short description:** Moonshot AI's mid-tier coding/agentic model, rolled out 2026-09-11 at the unchanged `kimi-for-coding` model ID in Kimi Code (replacing K2.7 Code). Vendor positions it "close to K3" with more efficient thinking, but publishes no parameters, benchmarks, weights, or per-token price.
- **Provider / access:** Kimi Code only (CLI, VS Code, Desktop, third-party agents via Kimi Code API keys — OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible base URLs). Included in membership plans (Plus+ new plans, Andante+ legacy). Not on Moonshot's Open Platform pay-as-you-go API.
- **Release / knowledge:** Rolled out 2026-09-11; knowledge cutoff not published.
- **IDs:** `kimi-for-coding` (Kimi Code route; the name "K2.8 Preview" is not a usable ID).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens (all plans with Kimi Code).
- **Modalities:** text + image + video input; text / tool-calls / code output; reasoning effort low/high/max (default max; `none` routes to K2.8 no-thinking). No open weights.
- **Pricing:** No official per-token API price; membership quota billing. Unofficial reseller listings (ZenMux, APIMaster) show $1 in / $4 out / $0.25 cache read — not documented by Moonshot.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed (likely shares K2.7 Code's MoE design per shared endpoint — inference, not confirmed).

## Raw benchmarks found

- **No verified public benchmark scores exist for this checkpoint** (as of 2026-11-06): no SWE-bench/GPQA/HLE or other numbers from Moonshot or independent evaluators; no Artificial Analysis page.
- Vendor statement only: performance "close to K3" (K3's own 93.5% GPQA Diamond figure does NOT carry over to this checkpoint).
- The only numeric third-party signals found: ZenMux measured ~41.1 tok/s throughput / 1.43s latency (a live metric, not a benchmark).

## Negative-findings notes

- Treat any quoted K2.8 benchmark score as unverified until Moonshot or an independent evaluator publishes one with a method.
- The model behind `kimi-for-coding` changed without a version bump on 2026-09-11 — pin evaluations and effort levels explicitly.
- No open weights and no system/model card; retention/training-on-inputs behavior unanswered.
- Use only if already on a Kimi plan with Kimi Code and you need 1M-context coding help at lower quota cost than K3; otherwise prefer K3 or K2.7 Code (both with public benchmarks/open weights).

